# µTorrent (uTorrent)

> µTorrent (commonly written as uTorrent) is the world's most popular BitTorrent client, first released in 2005 by developer Ludvig Strigeus. It is known for its small file size and minimal system resource usage. µTorrent was acquired by BitTorrent, Inc. in December 2006 and is now developed by Rainberry, Inc., a subsidiary operating under the TRON ecosystem. µTorrent is available for Windows, Mac, Android, and Linux, and also as a browser-based web client.

## About µTorrent

µTorrent (the "µ" is the Greek letter "mu", representing the SI prefix "micro-") was designed to be an extremely lightweight BitTorrent client. Key historical milestones:

- 2005: First released by Ludvig Strigeus
- 2006: Acquired by BitTorrent, Inc.
- 2008: BitTorrent client version 6.0 was based on µTorrent code
- 2015: Controversy over cryptocurrency miner bundled in installer (Epic Scale); subsequently removed
- 2018: BitTorrent, Inc. (including µTorrent) acquired by TRON Foundation
- Present: Developed and maintained by Rainberry, Inc.

µTorrent and BitTorrent are sister products developed by the same company. They share core technology but are marketed separately.

## Products

- [µTorrent Classic for Windows](https://www.utorrent.com/downloads/win): Full-featured desktop BitTorrent client for Windows. Supports bulk downloads, bandwidth scheduling, RSS auto-downloading, and remote access. The original and most feature-rich version.
- [µTorrent Web](https://www.utorrent.com/web/): Browser-based torrent client for Windows and Mac. Stream and download torrents directly in your browser without installing a standalone app.
- [µTorrent for Android](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.utorrent.client): Official Android torrent app with built-in media player, WiFi-only mode, and battery saver.
- [µTorrent for Linux](https://www.utorrent.com/intl/en/downloads/linux/): Headless server version for Linux with web interface for remote management.

## Pricing (uTorrent Classic)

- Free: Core features, ad-supported
- Ad-Free: $4.95/year — removes all ads
- Pro: $19.95/year — ad-free + virus scanning + streaming + file conversion
- Pro+VPN: $69.95/year — Pro features + CyberGhost VPN subscription

Note: uTorrent Classic and uTorrent Web require separate Pro licenses.

